==English==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{L.}} ''[[femininus|féminīnus]]'', from ''[[femina|fémina]]'' (woman). (See ''[[feminine]]''). ''Feminist'' first recorded in English 1894, from French ''[[féministe]]'' (1872). See also ''[[feminism]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ˈfɛmənɪst/}}
*{{SAMPA|/"fEm@nIst/}}

===Adjective===
'''feminist'''

# Relating to or in accordance with [[feminism]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who supports the equality of women with men.
# A member of a feminist political movement.
# One who believes in the social, political, and economoical equality of the sexes.

